more *perceptual* "how much did it change" number a musician might also want on screen, and it's
cheap — so the job's "calibrate both" instinct was right: keep ‖z0‖ as a readout, but the KNOB
is ‖dt·v‖. **Caveat:** this is the GUIDANCE-path gain (TFG/LatCH); the `sa3_control` ADAPTER
gain (~6, forward FiLM) is a separate mechanism this normalization doesn't touch — don't
conflate them. Since it's a product-knob decision, I'm putting the ‖z0‖-vs-‖dt·v‖ call to Kim
